# Emergency braking (docs/emergency_stop.md) on the burn-in axis (10 mm a
# revolution; 1 rad = 1.59 mm). hv0.sim_dist, zeroed at the failure, is how
# far the axis went.
# The dynamic brake with the DC bus high (above high_dc_volt; here set below
# the simulated 300 V supply): rv backs off to 0, a plain short, so no
# energy goes into the bus, although the current is then above the 1.8 A
# target. The short's transient (~3.4 A) stays above 1.3 x the target for
# 2 ms, so the brake then gives up: outputs off, coasting (the bus full and
# the current too high: nothing else is safe; ~10 rad, the few ms of
# braking before it gave up included).
@args --drive ../hwtest/burnin/ECMA-C30604FS/stmbl.conf
@timeout 120
lcnc 0 0
run 0.5
lcnc 1 0
run 1.5
lcnc 1 300
run 1
dbrake0.max_cur = 2
dbrake0.high_dc_volt = 250
hv0.sim_dist = 0
enc_fb0.sim_fail = 1
run 0.0024
@sample dbrake0.rv 0.0004 0.002
@sample hv0.abs_cur 0.0004 0.002
run 0.01
dbrake0.gave_up
fault0.en_out
run 0.4
hv0.sim_dist
@expect max dbrake0.rv < 0.001
@expect max|hv0.abs_cur| > 2.4
@expect dbrake0.gave_up == 1
@expect fault0.en_out == 0
@expect hv0.sim_dist > 8
